IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (TVRO System) Regulations (G.N. No. S 126/1991; Rg 3, 2004 Revised Edition), made under s 66 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-tvro-system-regulations-1991/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-RG3.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand;
-- a secondary source). Quotations below are lines of THAT file; `srcrefs.py` is run on this module against it.
-- Window: the text served is the 2004 Revised Edition; whether it was amended or revoked afterwards is not shown (sgba-vintage.l4).

§ `Regulation 2: Definitions`

-- src:6 | “broadcast television receiver” means any apparatus used for the visual and aural reception of any broadcasting service;
@ref reg 2 "broadcast television receiver" (src:6)
GIVEN `it is an apparatus used for the visual and aural reception of any broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the apparatus is a broadcast television receiver` MEANS
    `it is an apparatus used for the visual and aural reception of any broadcasting service`

-- src:7 | “institution” means any body of persons, corporate or unincorporate, and includes any undertaking;
@ref reg 2 "institution" (src:7)
-- "includes any undertaking": whether an individual who runs an undertaking is thereby an institution is a fork (F-BA-05).
GIVEN `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the person is an institution` MEANS
    `it is a body of persons, corporate or unincorporate` OR `it is an undertaking`

-- src:8 | “licence” means a licence to install or operate one or more TVRO systems;
@ref reg 2 "licence" (src:8)
GIVEN `it is a licence to install or operate one or more TVRO systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the licence is a licence within these Regulations` MEANS
    `it is a licence to install or operate one or more TVRO systems`

-- src:9 | “licensee” means a person to whom a licence is granted;
@ref reg 2 "licensee" (src:9)
GIVEN `a licence has been granted to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the person is a licensee` MEANS
    `a licence has been granted to the person`

-- src:10 | “telecommunications” has the same meaning as in the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323);
@ref reg 2 "telecommunications" (src:10)
-- Borrowed from the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323): the meaning is asked as a fact.
GIVEN `it is telecommunications within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the thing is telecommunications` MEANS
    `it is telecommunications within the meaning of the Telecommunications Act`

-- src:11 | “TVRO system” means any apparatus (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable of direct reception of broadcast matter emitted from or passing through any communication or broadcast satellite in extra-terrestrial space.
@ref reg 2 "TVRO system" (src:11)
GIVEN a IS A Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 the apparatus is a TVRO system` MEANS
    a's `capable of direct reception from a satellite`

§ `Regulation 3: Application and qualifications`

-- src:13 | 3. —(1) An application for a licence shall —
-- src:14 | ( a ) be made in such form and manner as the Authority may determine; and
-- src:15 | ( b ) contain a full and true account of such particulars as the Authority may require.
@ref reg 3(1) (src:13-15)
GIVEN `the application is made in the form and manner the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application contains a full and true account of the particulars the Authority required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(1) the application for a licence is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the application is made in the form and manner the Authority determined` AND `the application contains a full and true account of the particulars the Authority required`

-- src:16 | (2) No person other than an institution may be granted with a licence.
@ref reg 3(2) (src:16)
-- Dated: the window of the Regulations as deposited. NOTHING outside it. An institution is what reg 2 defines.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person is an institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2) the person may be granted a licence, on` MEANS
    IF `the TVRO System Regulations as deposited are the text in force on` d THEN JUST `the person is an institution` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 4: Licence fee`

-- src:18 | 4. —(1) The Authority may refuse to grant or renew any licence unless such fee as the Authority may determine to be levied in respect of the licence is paid.
@ref reg 4(1) (src:18)
GIVEN `the fee the Authority determined for the licence has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(1) the Authority may not refuse to grant or renew the licence for want of the fee` MEANS
    `the fee the Authority determined for the licence has been paid`

-- src:19 | (2) No fee or part thereof paid in respect of any licence granted by the Authority shall be refunded in respect of the unexpired period of any licence which has been cancelled or suspended in accordance with section 21, read with section 12, of the Act.
@ref reg 4(2) (src:19)
GIVEN `the licence was cancelled or suspended in accordance with section 21, read with section 12, of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2) any fee or part of a fee paid is refundable for the unexpired period` MEANS
    IF `the licence was cancelled or suspended in accordance with section 21, read with section 12, of the Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 5: Period of licence`

-- src:21 | 5. A licence shall be valid for such period as the Authority may determine unless it is sooner cancelled or suspended.
@ref reg 5 (src:21)
GIVEN `the date is within the period the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has been cancelled or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 5 the licence is valid` MEANS
    `the date is within the period the Authority determined` AND (NOT `the licence has been cancelled or suspended`)

§ `Regulation 6: Replacement of licence`

-- src:23 | 6. —(1) If the Authority is satisfied that any licence granted by it has been lost, destroyed or defaced, the Authority may, subject to paragraph (2), on payment of a fee of $2 issue a duplicate licence in place thereof.
@ref reg 6(1) (src:23)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied that the licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 6(1) the Authority may issue a duplicate licence on payment of the fee` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied that the licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced` AND `the fee paid` AT LEAST 2

-- src:24 | (2) No duplicate licence shall be issued under this regulation in place of a defaced licence unless the defaced licence is surrendered to the Authority for cancellation.
@ref reg 6(2) (src:24)
GIVEN `the licence is defaced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defaced licence has been surrendered to the Authority for cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 6(2) a duplicate licence may be issued` MEANS
    (NOT `the licence is defaced`) OR `the defaced licence has been surrendered to the Authority for cancellation`

§ `Regulations 7 to 9`

-- src:26 | 7. A licensee shall not transfer, assign or dispose of his licence.
@ref reg 7 (src:26)
GIVEN `the licensee transfers, assigns or disposes of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 7 the licensee has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee transfers, assigns or disposes of the licence`

-- src:28 | 8. A licensee shall inform the Authority in writing of any change to or inaccuracy in any of its particulars furnished to the Authority under regulation 3(1)( b ).
@ref reg 8 (src:28)
GIVEN `a particular furnished under regulation 3(1)(b) has changed or is inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has informed the Authority in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 8 the licensee has complied` MEANS
    IF `a particular furnished under regulation 3(1)(b) has changed or is inaccurate` THEN JUST `the licensee has informed the Authority in writing` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:30 | 9. A person whose licence is cancelled or suspended under section 21, read with section 12, of the Act shall, if required by the Authority, surrender the licence to the Authority within such time as the Authority may specify.
@ref reg 9 (src:30)
GIVEN `the licence was cancelled or suspended under section 21, read with section 12, of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority requires surrender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 9 the person must surrender the licence within the time the Authority specifies` MEANS
    IF `the licence was cancelled or suspended under section 21, read with section 12, of the Act` THEN JUST `the Authority requires surrender` ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 10: Installation diagrams, etc.`

-- src:32 | 10. A licensee of a TVRO system shall, within 14 days of the installation of the TVRO system in respect of which the licence is granted, furnish the following to the Authority:
-- src:33 | ( a ) a diagram or diagrams showing the location of the TVRO system installed and the cable distribution system connecting the TVRO system to broadcast television receivers;
-- src:34 | ( b ) particulars of the type and model of the apparatus constituting the TVRO system; and
-- src:35 | ( c ) the location of every broadcast television receiver that the licensee has caused to be connected to the TVRO system.
@ref reg 10(a) to (c) (src:32-35)
GIVEN `the days since the installation` IS A NUMBER
      `the licensee has furnished a diagram of the location of the system and the cable distribution system connecting it to broadcast television receivers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has furnished particulars of the type and model of the apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has furnished the location of every broadcast television receiver the licensee has caused to be connected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 10 the licensee has furnished what the regulation requires in time` MEANS
    `the days since the installation` AT MOST 14
    AND `the licensee has furnished a diagram of the location of the system and the cable distribution system connecting it to broadcast television receivers`
    AND `the licensee has furnished particulars of the type and model of the apparatus`
    AND `the licensee has furnished the location of every broadcast television receiver the licensee has caused to be connected`

§ `Regulations 11 to 14: Operation, agreements, modification, non-operation`

-- src:37 | 11. —(1) No TVRO system shall be operated in a manner which interferes or may interfere with the efficient or convenient operation or maintenance of any telephone, telegraph or power line which existed at the time of installation of such TVRO system.
@ref reg 11(1) (src:37)
GIVEN `the system is operated in a manner which interferes or may interfere with the efficient or convenient operation or maintenance of a telephone, telegraph or power line which existed at the time of installation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11(1) the operation is prohibited` MEANS
    `the system is operated in a manner which interferes or may interfere with the efficient or convenient operation or maintenance of a telephone, telegraph or power line which existed at the time of installation`

-- src:38 | (2) No licensee shall operate any TVRO system in such manner as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by any other broadcasting apparatus licensed under the Act or the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323).
@ref reg 11(2) (src:38)
GIVEN `the licensee operates the system in such a manner as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by other broadcasting apparatus licensed under the Act or the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11(2) the operation is prohibited` MEANS
    `the licensee operates the system in such a manner as knowingly to cause interference or disturbance to reception by other broadcasting apparatus licensed under the Act or the Telecommunications Act`

-- src:39 | (3) No licensee shall intercept any signal, sign, writing, image, sound or intelligence of any nature transmitted which is not intended for reception by the general public.
@ref reg 11(3) (src:39)
GIVEN `the licensee intercepts a signal, sign, writing, image, sound or intelligence not intended for reception by the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 11(3) the interception is prohibited` MEANS
    `the licensee intercepts a signal, sign, writing, image, sound or intelligence not intended for reception by the general public`

-- src:41 | 12. A licensee shall, in the installation or operation of a TVRO system, observe the provisions of the International Telecommunication Convention and any bilateral or multilateral telecommunication agreements in force and the regulations pertaining to the operation of TVRO systems that are made under that Convention and agreements.
@ref reg 12 (src:41)
GIVEN `the licensee observes the International Telecommunication Convention, bilateral or multilateral telecommunication agreements in force, and the regulations under them pertaining to TVRO systems` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 12 the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the licensee observes the International Telecommunication Convention, bilateral or multilateral telecommunication agreements in force, and the regulations under them pertaining to TVRO systems`

-- src:43 | 13. —(1) A licensee of a TVRO system shall not —
-- src:44 | ( a ) modify or alter any apparatus constituting the TVRO system; or
-- src:45 | ( b ) change the location of that TVRO system, except with the approval of the Authority.
@ref reg 13(1) (src:43-45)
GIVEN `the licensee modifies or alters apparatus constituting the system, or changes its location` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 13(1) the licensee has breached the regulation` MEANS
    `the licensee modifies or alters apparatus constituting the system, or changes its location` AND (NOT `the Authority has approved`)

-- src:46 | (2) If there is any change in the number of broadcast television receivers in his possession connected to a TVRO system or a change in the location of any such broadcast television receiver, the licensee of that TVRO system shall immediately inform the Authority in writing of such change.
@ref reg 13(2) (src:46)
GIVEN `there is a change in the number of broadcast television receivers in the licensee's possession connected to the system, or in the location of any of them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has immediately informed the Authority in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 13(2) the licensee has complied` MEANS
    IF `there is a change in the number of broadcast television receivers in the licensee's possession connected to the system, or in the location of any of them` THEN JUST `the licensee has immediately informed the Authority in writing` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:48 | 14. When a licensee ceases to operate the TVRO system in respect of which his licence is granted, he shall not sell, offer for sale or otherwise dispose of the TVRO system or any part thereof except with the approval of the Authority.
@ref reg 14 (src:48)
GIVEN `the licensee has ceased to operate the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee sells, offers for sale or otherwise disposes of the system or a part of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 14 the licensee has breached the regulation` MEANS
    IF `the licensee has ceased to operate the system` THEN JUST (`the licensee sells, offers for sale or otherwise disposes of the system or a part of it` AND (NOT `the Authority has approved`)) ELSE NOTHING
